  "id": "DrugBank_DB04572 - MONDO_3792",
  "verbalization": "Thiotepa, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Ovarian Carcinosarcoma through a series of indirect pathways involving germ cell tumors. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa may act as a therapeutic agent in the treatment of immature ovarian teratoma, malignant dysgerminomatous germ cell tumor of the ovary, and other related tumors, which in turn are associated with Melphalan, another chemotherapy drug. This chain of indications implies a potential role for Thiotepa in the management of ovarian carcinomas, possibly through shared mechanisms of action or systemic effects that influence tumor progression. The presence of multiple pathways linking Thiotepa to Ovarian Carcinosarcoma underscores the possibility of a broader therapeutic relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader context of drug-target interactions in oncology.",
